@dwex
title: CV-05 - Convoyer survives a non-dislodging attack
desc:  Gilgamesch B.3.2.12 only dissolves the convoy if the fleet is
       actually dislodged. Here ENG attacks NTH unsupported, but NTH
       receives hold-support from MID (legal because a con order is not
       a movement order, B.3.1.2). NTH defends with strength 2, ENG
       attacks with strength 1, the attack bounces, the convoy chain
       stays intact and the army arrives.

map {
  Lon LCB 0, 0.0
  NTH O   2, 0.6
  Bel LC  4, 0.0
  ENG O   2,-0.6
  MID O   4, 0.6
  Lon --F NTH
  NTH --F Bel
  ENG --F NTH
  MID --F NTH
}

orders {
  En A Lon mve Bel
  En F NTH con Lon
  En F MID hsup NTH
  Ge F ENG mve NTH !
}
@end
